## Founding & History
Dalrymple Vineyards was established in 1987. It was founded by David Morris or by the Mitchell and Sundstrup families. Specifically, Bertel and Anne Sundstrup, along with Anne's sister Jill Mitchell, established Dalrymple in 1987, encouraged by Dominique Portet of Taltarni Vineyard. The Sundstrups were inspired by travels to France and planted vines on the sloping hills of Pipers River, overlooking Bass Strait.

In late 2007, Hill-Smith Family Vineyards acquired the vineyard and brand from the Mitchell and Sundstrup families. In December 2012, Hill-Smith Family Vineyards further acquired a 120-hectare property, which included the original Frogmore Creek Vineyard, with 10 hectares designated for Dalrymple's Pinot Noir, known as the Mount Lord Vineyard.

## People
Peter Caldwell has been the vigneron, responsible for viticulture and winemaking at Dalrymple Vineyards since 2010. Born and raised in Tasmania on a sheep and cattle farm, Caldwell developed an interest in winemaking after working at Heemskerk (now Jansz) in Pipers River. He studied winemaking and viticulture at Roseworthy College in South Australia. Before joining Dalrymple, he spent nearly two decades gaining experience in Bordeaux, Burgundy, California, and New Zealand, including 10 years at Te Kairanga Wines in New Zealand and two years with Josef Chromy Wines. Caldwell is particularly passionate about Pinot Noir.

## Vineyard & Site
Dalrymple Vineyards is located in the Pipers River region of Tasmania. The vineyards are situated on sloping hills overlooking Bass Strait. The region benefits from a cool climate and maritime influence from Bass Strait, with cool breezes from surrounding hills creating a microclimate suitable for elegant, aromatic wines. The soils across the estate vary, including sandy loams, clay, and gravel.

The total vineyard area is 17 hectares. Dalrymple cultivates varietals such as Pinot Noir, Chardonnay, Pinot Gris, and Sauvignon Blanc. The winery also sources grapes from other Tasmanian regions, including Ouse and Swansea, which offer different climatic conditions and produce distinct wines. In 2012, Hill-Smith Family Vineyards acquired the 120-hectare property where the original Frogmore Creek Vineyard was established, with 10 hectares dedicated to Pinot Noir for Dalrymple, known as the Mount Lord Vineyard.

## Cellar Door Experience
Dalrymple Vineyards offers tastings by appointment only. Bookings are essential and require at least 24 hours' notice, as the winery is not staffed daily for visitors. The tasting experience takes place in a private tasting room or the winery lab, offering an intimate and authentic experience. Visitors can taste award-winning wines, learn about the single site program, and gain insight into the winemaking process from Peter Caldwell. A "Dalrymple Behind the Scenes Tasting" is offered, lasting approximately 40 minutes.

The winery also offers a self-guided tour around the vineyard with four audio posts providing insights into the vineyard and region. As of a recent update, wine room tastings are currently unavailable.

## Food & Hospitality
Dalrymple Vineyards does not appear to have a permanent restaurant or kitchen for daily service. However, they have hosted special events that include food. For example, the "Dalrymple Unearthed: A Rare Pinot Experience" event in May 2025 included canapés on arrival, a seasonal long lunch featuring locally sourced produce, and shared Tasmanian cheese boards. Return transport from Launceston was included for this event.

## Awards & Recognition
Dalrymple Vineyards has received recognition for its wines. The Dalrymple Vineyards Mt. Lord Pinot Noir 2022 was awarded Top Rated Pinot Noir and 96 Points in the Halliday Wine Companion. The winery has been rated as a five-star winery by Halliday, indicating it is an "Outstanding winery capable of producing wines of very high quality" and typically has at least two wines rated 95 points or above.

Other Halliday Wine Companion scores include:
* Single Site Coal River Valley Pinot Noir 2023: 95 Points
* Single Site Ouse Pinot Noir 2023: 95 Points
* Single Site Estate Pipers River Pinot Noir 2023: 94 Points
* Single Site Estate Coal River Chardonnay 2023: 94 Points
* Single Site Estate Pipers River Chardonnay 2022: 93 Points
* Tasmanian Pinot Noir 2023: 93 Points

The winery has also received a Platinum award at the Decanter World Wine Awards in 2023. The Real Review lists Dalrymple with 10 Gold Ribbons, 22 Silver Ribbons, 11 Bronze Ribbons, and 11 Top Ranks.

